From 73c2c17e6d46d319d1d61730847195c8210e97f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:02:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(goldens): check runs qualifier review and fails closed;
 --no-qualifier

Spec rule 11 says check runs qualifier review; toolpath's check did not
run it at all. It now runs `qualifier review` in the repo root
(binary from $TOOLPATH_GOLDENS_QUALIFIER, else PATH) and fails on a
non-zero exit or any drifted or missing anchor. Unlike pathbase (which
skips with an info line), a missing binary is a FAILURE unless
`--no-qualifier` is passed, which records the skip as an info row.

The cargo goldens test opts out explicitly when no binary is found (the
dev shell does not ship qualifier); the producer-pin tests opt out because
their throwaway repo has no records. Documented in goldens/DEMO.md.
---
 crates/path-cli/src/goldens.rs            | 88 +++++++++++++++++++++++
