From baa5e0572dd773261e7c8a3b0673eefa78c9a723 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:48:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(goldens): only the input and the outputs can fail a set

check treated Cargo.lock, flake.lock, the toolchain pin, the goldens source files
and the captured repo_rev as pins, so a lockfile bump, a doc edit or a squash
merge turned every set red, and a one-commit CI checkout could never pass
(repo_rev is not in HEAD's history there). Those are now recorded per set as
`environment` and reported as info when they move; an environment change that
alters an output still fails on that output's sha. A dev build's binary path
and a live-captured agent's path are no longer written (they named the
developer's home); a nix store path still is. toolpath-golden is a
dev-dependency (tests/roundtrip.rs only), so path-cli packages again without a
version for it.
